1. SG15 ONCV pseudopotential
2. symmetry=on
3. test LDOS with 2 eV, output ldos_2ev.cube

Reference precision validation (2026-10-26)

The original scf_thr=1e-9 input left solver-dependent LDOS values above the
existing pointwise 1e-8 file-comparison tolerance. This fixture now uses
scf_thr=1e-12 and pw_diag_thr=1e-12, with 200 iterations available for each
solver loop and diago_smooth_ethr=false. The structure, pseudopotential,
band count, grid, bias and acceptance tolerances are unchanged.

The energy and LDOS reference were generated by a fresh CG calculation.
Independent CG, Davidson-subspace and PPCG calculations with four MPI ranks
and OMP_NUM_THREADS=OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 all converged.
The maximum pairwise energy difference was 1.05e-8 eV; all 729 grid values
agreed within 1e-10 and passed the original 1e-8 pointwise comparator.
Cube headers and grids matched, all values were finite, and the maximum
integral difference was 1.13e-11. PPCG reported no residual warnings.

All three converged results differed from the previous energy reference by
about 3e-7 eV and from its cube values by up to 1e-4. Updating both references
therefore records the stricter calculation, without changing the comparator.
The reference calculation used base commit 77f7b4af6 plus the local solver
stability changes; executable SHA256:
d9d2914b9f8f793d0da52f28b09a6996ae39483958658dfb72490f51c2b842f1.

To reproduce the cross-solver check, copy this fixture into clean directories,
set ks_solver to cg, dav_subspace and ppcg respectively, and run the original
Autotest.sh with -n4 -o1. Keep the same reference files and tolerances.
